# Code owners for pwrap.
#
# This file is required, not decorative. The `only-berke-push` ruleset on the
# default branch sets require_code_owner_review, and without a CODEOWNERS file
# there are no code owners — so that requirement can never be satisfied by a
# review, and every pull request, including Dependabot's, is unmergeable except
# by an admin bypass. A global owner restores normal review-and-merge.
#
# Last match wins, so keep the catch-all first and narrow rules below it.

*       @b3vet

# Release and CI plumbing: publishing credentials and the trusted-publisher
# contract live here, so changes deserve a deliberate look.
/.github/workflows/    @b3vet

# Published SDK surface — anything here reaches users through npm, PyPI or the
# Go module proxy, where a released version can never be taken back.
/sdk/                  @b3vet

# Tenant and control-plane SQL. Migrations are append-only once applied.
/migrations/           @b3vet
